diff --git a/doc/fastwam.md b/doc/fastwam.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..2984927e62456132fa179d2d75c546487a131586
--- /dev/null
+++ b/doc/fastwam.md
@@ -0,0 +1,126 @@
+# Experimental FastWAM native fixed profile
+
+**Not functionally accepted.** This isolated port was developed under an
+explicit no-tests/no-extra-review instruction. Building, registering, preparing
+or measuring it must not be represented as passing operator or public API gates.
+Actual full native/public benchmark evidence exists (job329256); it is recorded
+below without treating saved-output arithmetic as a new test/acceptance gate.
+
+## Declared seam
+
+Native BF16 SM80 only. LIBERO checkpoint `libero_uncond_2cam224.pt`, author
+revision `7faa71108368fbb3b6885649f112af607427a2d4`; H32/A7, proprio8,
+normalized resized single current image224x448, cachedT5[128,4096], Euler20,
+sigma_shift5. Cached text encoding is explicitly outside the measured graph;
+image VAE, VideoDiT30, proprio projection, text embedding/crossKV, ActionDiT30
+and all20 solver steps are inside one graph.
+
+Image input is floating normalized NHWC[224,448,3], or its declared packed
+[100352,3] representation through the generic binding. Context features use
+`VlaMetadata.language_features`; token slots have length128 and mask128.
+Caller-provided noise[32,7] is required; generated noise is explicitly unsupported.
+Output is normalized BF16 actions[32,7], transferred to FP32 only at the public
+output boundary. This policy is not a deployable robot action adapter.
+
+## Ownership and entry points
+
+- `fastwam/load.rs`: existing Rust registry/AutoModel loader.
+- `fastwam/model.rs`: forward order, fixed flow schedule, time conditioning.
+- `fastwam/vision.rs`: WanVAE38 first-frame encoder semantics.
+- `fastwam/runner.rs`: input binding, stable arena, graph and output lifetime.
+- `FastWamPolicy`: existing AutoPolicy/ModelRunner integration; generic
+  `_infer_preprocessed(...,language_features=context)` binding.
+
+Checkpoint export is one-time CPU weight mapping, not inference. It transposes
+linears, reduces zero-history T1 causal3d kernels to their last temporal slice,
+and retains full spatial kernels. The first temporal-downsample time_conv is
+intentionally bypassed, matching the author's cache-first-frame path. Decoder
+weights and the unused video output head are not loaded.
+
+Fixed schedule modulation is computed by native GPU operators during setup.
+Per-request text K/V and video K/V are reused within the action loop, not across
+unrelated observations. All forward intermediates stay on GPU. Graph output
+aliases reusable storage; consumers must download/copy before the next replay.
+
+## Precision / performance debt
+
+The safe spatial baseline adds channel L2 BF16 normalization, NHWC im2col,
+first-frame grouped averages, adjacent-pair RoPE and masked BF16 attention.
+It is native, but untested at the operator level and untuned. FP32 cos/sin tables with FP64 rotary
+products differ from the author's FP64 table representation; output comparisons
+must quantify the effect. Welford LayerNorm, whole3072 RMSNorm and BF16 rounding
+boundaries are explicit. No FP8 is used on A800.
+
+Preparation warms up the actual complete model before capture. Public
+`prepare_for` is supported; shape-only preparation and unsupported devices,
+precisions, dimensions and schedule overrides fail explicitly. A native family
+benchmark executable alone is not proof that the Python policy was exercised.
+
+## Recorded complete native result (not release acceptance)
+
+Slurm329256 completed on2026-11-15,23:49:42->23:51:05+08:00,exit0, A800-SXM4-80GB,
+driver580.178.04 (`logs/full-native-329256.log:5`). Both native and existing public AutoPolicy/binding paths saved
+80outputs (eight formal cases x10). No tests, smoke/operator suites or extra
+reviews were run. No additional model execution is implied by these notes.
+
+| Timing scope | Median ms | Mean ms | P95 ms |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|
+| Whole graph dispatch/completion wall |212.5182835|212.6541041875|213.09412235|
+| Prepared-input upload + graph + output wall |212.869315|213.018002175|213.75278815|
+| Public AutoPolicy wall |215.3436585795|215.5860788247|216.6182828136|
+
+Saved-output arithmetic versus author compiled20 and project compiled20 from
+source227993d5/job327380: maxrelL2 0.011609512347092753, mincosine
+0.9999326109645393, maxabs0.05078125. Both paths are within the original
+0.05/0.999 numerical proxy. This is not an independent operator/capture-parity
+gate, deployment acceptance or robot-success evidence.
+
+The public benchmark receives CPU FP32 NHWC prepared before timing; historical
+project timing receives NCHW. Keep that seam difference explicit and calculate
+no pure-backend speedup ratio. New latency is slower than historical author
+142.4363065ms and project137.6502975ms: this implementation is **not the winner**.
+Whole-graph dispatch/completion wall is not a pure CUDA-event kernel duration.
+
+Native preparation is27,855.473494ms excluding eight warmup replays. Public
+preparation15,204.954596ms includes eight warmups and has different cache/process
+conditions; these are not matching cold-start measurements. Arena consumption
+is4,595,864,768bytes within12GiB, not a measured live activation peak.
+
+Portable source-only reproduction helpers and build/asset instructions:
+[`python/apxinf/examples/fastwam_experimental/`](../python/apxinf/examples/fastwam_experimental/README.md).
+Those helper adapters/documentation were curated after measurement, not rerun.
+
+## Source-visible performance debt (not profiling)
+
+These are implementation facts and hypotheses for later authorized work, not
+measured stage percentages, causal attribution of the latency gap, or promised
+speedups:
+
+1. `model.rs::attention` reuses maintained FA2 only for same-length unmasked
+   attention. Action self-attention has32queries/130keys and uses the custom
+   baseline, as does masked text cross-attention. The custom CUDA implementation
+   performs warp FP32 dot reduction, stores per-row probabilities, then loops
+   serially over keys for each output channel; it does not use a tiled
+   Tensor-Core/FlashAttention implementation. Static forward order calls this
+   action self/cross pair600times each, video cross30times and VAE once per
+   request. Those counts are source-derived, not measured timings.
+2. Action K/V are concatenated with98cached video tokens inside every one of
+   600action blocks. Two130x3072BF16 concatenations imply958,464,000logical
+   output bytes per request, plus corresponding reads; this is **not measured
+   DRAM traffic**. Video KV and text cross-KV are already request-cached; do not
+   describe those caches as missing. A fixed-prefix/action-window layout could
+   remove repeated concatenation but has no measured benefit here.
+3. WanVAE convolutions materialize NHWC im2col matrices and then invoke GEMM and
+   a separate bias operation. This is a complete native path, not a tuned
+   convolution provider. No cuDNN/fused-convolution comparison was performed.
+4. LayerNorm, scale/shift, Q/K RMS, adjacent RoPE, activation and residual/gating
+   remain many distinct device operations with intermediate BF16 boundaries.
+   CUDA Graph removes repeated host construction/submission, not those kernels
+   or their intermediate traffic. Fusion must preserve intended rounding;
+   no post-measurement fusion or numerical acceptance is claimed.
+5. `runner.rs` deliberately uses `without_autotune` and a monotonic graph arena.
+   Missing GEMM tuning and cross-node buffer liveness reuse are performance
+   debt; the4.596GB logical arena consumption is observed, but its latency
+   contribution is unmeasured. Policy validation/copies/FP32->BF16 conversion,
+   synchronization before input update and final output transfer are additional
+   public-seam work, not proof that they explain the native-vs-historical gap.
