+# Experimental FastWAM reproduction sources
+
+These sources reproduce the fixed LIBERO path described in
+[`doc/fastwam.md`](../../../../doc/fastwam.md). **Experimental, not deployable,
+not functionally/release accepted.** No tests or extra reviews were run under
+the original user's waiver. Actual complete native/public inference and saved
+output arithmetic exist; they do not waive the missing independent gates.
+
+## Source and assets
+
+Apply the supplied source patch to the **full archived foundation content**,
+not just its Git HEAD: the foundation includes uncommitted private changes.
+Foundation base Git HEAD is `7f37642dd6c5896bca66d7640d9944c2a3fe04b4`.
+This delta depends on that archived private Hy foundation; it is not a
+self-contained clean7f37642 rebuild. Do not publish the whole dirty foundation.
+The source patch and its manifest identify the exact archive and content hashes.
+
+Reference author revision: `7faa71108368fbb3b6885649f112af607427a2d4`.
+The intended assets are the exact author `libero_uncond_2cam224.pt` and
+`Wan2.2_VAE.pth` identified by the exporter's SHA256 allowlist. Checkpoint data,
+raw inputs/actions, environments, native archives and binary executables are
+**not** included. Obtain/reuse those assets separately subject to their licenses.
+Do not substitute another checkpoint variant. Author MIT license/NOTICE live in
+`crates/apxinf-model/src/fastwam/`; the foundation Apache-2.0 LICENSE is retained.
+
+## One-time CPU preparation
+
+Requirements for these offline exporters: Python with NumPy, SafeTensors and
+PyTorch. PyTorch is used only for trusted checkpoint/layout conversion, never
+as the native model's inference engine. Use existing approved environments;
+these scripts do not install anything or contact a service.
+
+From the patched repository root, use your own output directory and existing
+asset/input locations (the shell variables below are caller-supplied):
+
+```bash
+HELPERS=python/apxinf/examples/fastwam_experimental
+python "$HELPERS/prepare_checkpoint.py" \
+  --checkpoint "$AUTHOR_LIBERO_PT" --vae "$AUTHOR_WAN_VAE_PTH" \
+  --output "$OWN_OUTPUT/checkpoint"
+python "$HELPERS/prepare_inputs.py" \
+  --npz-dir "$FORMAL_EIGHT_CASE_NPZ_DIR" --output "$OWN_OUTPUT/inputs"
+```
+
+The output directories must be empty. The input helper expects the same eight
+named formal cases as the Rust benchmark; it generates no synthetic samples.
+Image NCHW->NHWC happens on CPU **before timing**. Mask storage is FP32 binary
+because the foundation safetensors loader rejects I8 file entries; the native
+runtime still uses I8 masks. Exported weights are BF16; causal3d zero-history T1
+selects the last temporal slice, with no general multi-frame claim.
+
+## Build only (no tests or smoke/import invocation)
+
+The observed build used Rust1.95.0, GCC11.4.0, CUDA12.8, SM80, Python3.11.
+Use a matching approved toolchain and an owned target/cache location:
+
+`build_native.sh` is a separately identified PUBLIC path-parameterized copy of
+the private task build commands. It requires explicit `FASTWAM_TASK_ROOT`,
+`APXINF_SOURCE_ROOT`, `APXINF_TOOLCHAIN_CARGO_HOME`,
+`APXINF_TOOLCHAIN_RUSTUP_HOME` and, for Python, `APPROVED_NATIVE_PYTHON`.
+It contains no private machine/account paths and has **not** been newly run.
+The direct build commands below are an alternative; neither approach submits
+jobs, performs model inference, or establishes a new acceptance gate.
+
+```bash
+export APXINF_CUDA_ARCH=sm_80
+export CARGO_TARGET_DIR="$OWN_OUTPUT/target"
+export PYO3_PYTHON="$APPROVED_NATIVE_PYTHON"
+cargo build --release --offline --locked -p apxinf-model --features cuda \
+  --example fastwam_bench
+cargo build --release --offline --locked -p apxinf-py \
+  --features cuda,extension-module
+```
+
+The measured build reused unchanged foundation native archives read-only using
+`APXINF_FOUNDATION_CUDA_BUILD` and `APXINF_FOUNDATION_CUDA_NEW_BUILD`, each naming
+a build directory with `output` metadata and `out/lib*.a`. Only use matching
+content-addressed foundation artifacts; see the accompanying build-identity
+notes. Leave both variables unset to compile the foundation native sources and
+the new spatial primitives normally. The from-source fallback was **not** the
+recorded build and has not been rerun. New spatial CUDA code compiles into the
+owned target directory in either path. No FP8 or external inference engine runs.
+
+For a direct source-tree Python bridge, stage the newly built extension into
+an owned directory without modifying an old environment:
+
+```bash
+mkdir -p "$OWN_OUTPUT/py-native"
+cp "$CARGO_TARGET_DIR/release/libapxinf_py.so" "$OWN_OUTPUT/py-native/apxinf_py.so"
+export PYTHONPATH="$OWN_OUTPUT/py-native:$PWD/python/apxinf"
+export PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1
+```
+
+## Actual full-model inference benchmarks — only when separately authorized
+
+**Do not execute these now under a no-more-GPU instruction.** When authorized,
+run model computation only within an allocated GPU step. On the observed
+cluster the bounded pattern was partition `gpu_a800`, one node/task, `--gres=gpu:1`,
+`--time=00:30:00`, `srun -n1 -c8 --cpu-bind=cores`; no automatic submission
+script is included. Never run model computation on a login node.
+
+```bash
+srun -n1 -c8 --cpu-bind=cores "$CARGO_TARGET_DIR/release/examples/fastwam_bench" \
+  "$OWN_OUTPUT/checkpoint" "$OWN_OUTPUT/inputs" "$OWN_OUTPUT/full-native.json"
+srun -n1 -c8 --cpu-bind=cores "$APPROVED_NATIVE_PYTHON" -B -u \
+  "$HELPERS/benchmark_policy.py" --checkpoint "$OWN_OUTPUT/checkpoint" \
+  --npz-dir "$FORMAL_EIGHT_CASE_NPZ_DIR" --output "$OWN_OUTPUT/public-policy.json"
+```
+
+Both source benchmarks exercise VAE38 + VideoDiT30 + ActionDiT30xEuler20 and
+save80outputs after8warmups, not an isolated operator or smoke workload.
+Cached T5 input is explicitly outside the graph. The native report separates
+whole-graph dispatch/completion wall and prepared-input/graph/output wall. The
+public report includes policy conversion/native binding/output work, but the
+CPU FP32 NHWC layout has already been prepared. Historical project timing takes
+NCHW, so do not present a pure-backend speedup ratio or matching seam claim.
+
+## Arithmetic on already saved outputs
+
+This command never loads a model or executes a test/reference task:
+
+```bash
+python "$HELPERS/compare_saved.py" --native "$OWN_OUTPUT/full-native.json" \
+  --public "$OWN_OUTPUT/public-policy.json" --author "$SAVED_AUTHOR_OUTPUTS_NPZ" \
+  --project "$SAVED_PROJECT_OUTPUTS_NPZ" --output "$OWN_OUTPUT/summary.json"
+```
+
+It reports the original0.05relative-L2/0.999cosine proxy without creating a new
+gate, and deliberately writes no raw actions to its aggregate report. The
+portable helper adapters were curated **after** job329256 and have not been
+rerun; measured runtime source hashes are unchanged and recorded separately.
